# shellcheck shell=bash disable=SC2034
# quarantine.env — the flaky tests set aside BY NAME (measured-console phase 15).
#
# A test that fails under load and passes alone is not deleted, not retried
# until green and not skipped in its file: it is listed here, with who owns
# fixing it and the day the quarantine ends. While a row stands, the phase
# tier's selection leaves the file out (runner/verify-select.ts) and the client
# suite excludes it (vite.config.ts); the release still runs every node and
# bats file. A row past its expiry FAILS `scripts/gates.sh` — the quick matrix
# too — so a quarantine is a loan, never a grave. The owner of the vocabulary
# is viewer/shared/quarantine-model.js; viewer/test/reds-ratchet.test.ts holds
# this file to it.
#
# One row per test file, TAB-separated:
#   id <TAB> owner <TAB> expires (YYYY-MM-DD, UTC; the last day it stands) <TAB> why
# id — <suite>:<path from the repository root>, suite one of node bats vitest playwright
#      (e.g. node:viewer/test/wait-count-raise.test.ts)
# owner — who fixes it: a phase (`measured-console/26`), an issue (`#441`) or a person
QUARANTINE_ROWS=''
